{
  "sn12.62:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.62 ",
  "sn12.62:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.62:0.3": "Unlearned (2nd) ",
  "sn12.62:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.62:1.2": "“Mendicants, an unlearned ordinary person might become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed from this body made up of the four principal states. ",
  "sn12.62:1.3": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.62:1.4": "This body made up of the four principal states is seen to accumulate and disperse, to be taken up and laid to rest. ",
  "sn12.62:1.5": "That’s why an unlearned ordinary person might become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed from it. ",
  "sn12.62:1.6": "But an unlearned ordinary person is unable to become disillusioned, dispassionate, or freed from that which is called ‘mind’ and also ‘sentience’ and also ‘consciousness’. ",
  "sn12.62:1.7": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.62:1.8": "Because for a long time they’ve been attached to it, thought of it as their own, and mistaken it: ",
  "sn12.62:1.9": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self.’ ",
  "sn12.62:1.10": "That’s why an unlearned ordinary person is unable to become disillusioned, dispassionate, or freed from it. ",
  "sn12.62:2.1": "But an unlearned ordinary person would be better off taking this body made up of the four principal states to be their self, rather than the mind. ",
  "sn12.62:2.2": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.62:2.3": "This body made up of the four principal states is seen to last for a year, or for two, three, four, five, ten, twenty, thirty,